//
// AN ASSERTED TEXT PARSE IS REFUSED (`@FR-N-Parse`, `@FR-N-Cast`): `s as integer` asserts a fit no text can
// prove, so `as integer?` is the spelling.
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard for a rule no test named; every cell answered as the
//   rule says on both backends on the tree it landed on.
// CHANNEL: the expected diagnostic.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the cast.
// HOLDS: every cell on both backends.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: a text parse `as integer` may fail

fn main() {
  s = "12";
  n: integer = s as integer;
  println("{n}");
}
